# Without a password, only requests addressed to this machine. A browser on the
# LAN, or a page on another site rebinding a name to it, is refused. The Host
# header is the sender's to choose, so this is not the lock against a client
# elsewhere: compose publishing on 127.0.0.1 is.
@elsewhere not host localhost 127.0.0.1 ::1
respond @elsewhere "SurfSense answers only on localhost until SURFSENSE_PASSWORD is set." 403
